AC is wildly overrated in rgrn, IMO.  You _really_ want it, but it
doesn't prevent instakills.  And the tactics you use in a protection
run will help you survive with somewhat worse AC against most
threats.  It's certainly very important, especially if you get swarmed
by elves or soldiers or whatever, but usually a few points of AC are
not what causes an avoidable death.
>
> Do you incorporate/recommend any type of restraint on increasing XL?

Not a hard limit, but I don't level up like a skyrocket.  If I can get
to minetown with low enough XL to make 2-3 protection purchases,
that's nice--but if I'm a wizard I'd rather get the extra PW and
damage from levelling up.   Kind of depends on the class and
situation, but basically if you move quickly and don't dilly-dally
then there's no reason to artificially restrict your levels.  Just
don't sit around levelling up without searching out your essentials
(PR, MR, SR, reflection, better armor, etc).



